<TextPageLayout title="Privacy" description="What SifterSearch keeps about you, why, and who processes it." updated="October 10, 2026" noindex={true}>
  <p>We keep as little as the service needs.</p>
  <h2>Without an account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your browser keeps a random identifier and your recent chat with Anís in local storage, so a conversation can continue.</li>
    <li>Our server keeps the messages you send Anís and his replies, with that identifier, to answer you and to improve him.</li>
    <li>Searches are logged (the query, not who you are) to measure and improve search.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>If you sign in</h2>
  <p>Signing in with Google gives us your email address and name. We use them to keep your conversations together across
    devices and to reply to you. We do not sell or share them for marketing.</p>
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>If you write to anis@oceanlibrary.com, we keep the letter and the reply. Every letter from us has a link to stop further
    mail.</p>
  <h2>How conversations are reviewed</h2>
  <p>Exchanges with Anís are checked afterwards — by AI models and sometimes by a person — to find wrong answers and weak
    searches. Conversations are not published without being anonymized.</p>
  <h2>Who processes data for us</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare (hosting, delivery, email routing), Amazon SES (email), Google (sign-in and some AI models), and the AI providers
    that power answers and checks (including Google, DeepSeek, OpenAI, Anthropic and TypeSafe). Payments for supporting the
    project are handled by Stripe; we never see card numbers.</p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>To have your conversations or account deleted, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>. See also the
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
</TextPageLayout>
